---
// PrismEducate — standalone product page (owner decision 2026-10-05,
// Launch-Manager DISPATCH-2026-10-05-three-products §3 and §4b).
//
// WHAT THIS PAGE MAY CLAIM, and why it is worded the way it is:
//
// PrismEducate's public build carries only permissively licensed data, so its
// atlas is smaller than its private build. Source of truth is that repo's own
// generated report, docs/evidence/2026-10-05-public-build-contents.md
// (PE-LIC-10, read 2026-10-05), NOT this page and NOT a hand-kept list:
//   - scrollable scans ship for Bowel, Kidneys, Liver, Lungs, Pancreas,
//     Prostate, Spine and Thyroid, after the owner accepted share-alike for
//     the abdominal collections on 2026-10-05 (that report, regenerated 22:37);
//   - the spine keeps its MRI conditions and loses its CT compressed-vertebra
//     pages, because `verse` is still held back (D245). Launch-Manager relayed
//     that the spine had both; the generated report says otherwise, and the
//     report is the authority — raised with it 2026-10-05;
//   - Brain, Breast and Heart ship published case-report figures but no
//     scrollable scans, and no decision changes that;
//   - every case-report figure is CC BY or CC0 and carries its citation.
//
// So: name the organs that have scrollable scans, never a count, and never
// promise a set size. A count would be falsified by the share-alike decision
// going either way; the names stay true.
//
// Downloads are behind EDUCATE_DOWNLOADS_LIVE, which is deliberately NOT the
// viewer's switch — see src/site-config.ts for why.
import Layout from "../layouts/Default.astro";
import { EDUCATE_DOWNLOADS_LIVE, API_BASE, EDUCATE_INSTALLER_PATH, WAITLIST_ENDPOINT } from "../site-config";

const educateEndpoint = API_BASE + EDUCATE_INSTALLER_PATH;
---

<Layout
  title="PrismEducate — MyBodyPrism"
  description="PrismEducate is a free educational atlas of real medical imaging: scroll through published scans, organ by organ, and see what each finding looks like."
>
  <section class="container narrow">
    <p class="eyebrow">Free, and its own download</p>
    <h1>PrismEducate</h1>

    <p class="lede">
      An atlas for learning what medical imaging actually looks like. Pick an
      organ, pick a condition, and look at real published scans — labelled and
      explained in plain words.
    </p>

    <h2>What's inside</h2>
    <p>
      Every organ in the atlas comes with figures from published case reports,
      each shown with the credit its licence asks for. For these organs you can
      also scroll through full scans, slice by slice, the way a radiologist
      would:
    </p>
    <ul class="organs">
      <li>Bowel</li>
      <li>Kidneys</li>
      <li>Liver</li>
      <li>Lungs</li>
      <li>Pancreas</li>
      <li>Prostate</li>
      <li>Spine</li>
      <li>Thyroid</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">
      The brain, breast and heart sections show published figures rather than
      scrollable scans: the scan collections for those organs aren't licensed
      for us to pass on to you. We'd rather ship a smaller atlas than one we
      don't have the right to give away. Where a licence allows more, more gets
      added.
    </p>
    <p>
      Everything here is somebody else's work, used under its own licence. The
      app lists every collection, its licence and the credit it asks for, on a
      screen you can open at any time.
    </p>

    <h2>What it is not</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      PrismEducate is for learning. It shows, labels and explains published
      imaging — it does not diagnose, and it is not a medical device. It is not
      a place to open your own scans: that's
      <a href="/pricing">the MyBodyPrism viewer</a>.
    </p>

    <h2>{EDUCATE_DOWNLOADS_LIVE ? "Get PrismEducate" : "Not available to download yet"}</h2>
    {
      EDUCATE_DOWNLOADS_LIVE ? (
        <form id="mbp-edu-form" novalidate>
          <label class="visually-hidden" for="mbp-edu-email">Email address</label>
          <input
            id="mbp-edu-email"
            type="email"
            name="email"
            placeholder="you@example.com"
            autocomplete="email"
            required
          />
          <button id="mbp-edu-btn" type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">
            Get PrismEducate
          </button>
          <p class="form-note">
            We'll use your email to follow up about your experience and tell you
            about updates — nothing else. See the
            <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
          </p>
          <p id="mbp-edu-error" class="form-error" hidden role="alert">
            Couldn't start the download. Check your email address and retry, or
            write to <a href="mailto:support@mybodyprism.com">support@mybodyprism.com</a>.
          </p>
          <p id="mbp-edu-ok" class="form-ok" hidden role="status">
            Your download is starting…
          </p>
        </form>
      ) : (
        <form id="mbp-edu-waitlist-form" action={WAITLIST_ENDPOINT} method="POST" novalidate>
          <input type="hidden" name="product" value="PrismEducate" />
          <label class="visually-hidden" for="mbp-edu-waitlist-email">Email address</label>
          <input
            id="mbp-edu-waitlist-email"
            type="email"
            name="email"
            placeholder="you@example.com"
            autocomplete="email"
            required
          />
          <button id="mbp-edu-waitlist-btn" type="submit" class="btn btn-primary">
            Tell me when it's ready
          </button>
          <p class="form-note">
            We'll email you once when PrismEducate is ready to download — nothing
            else. See the <a href="/legal/privacy">Privacy Policy</a>.
          </p>
          <p id="mbp-edu-waitlist-error" class="form-error" hidden role="alert">
            Couldn't add you to the list. Check your email address and retry, or
            write to <a href="mailto:support@mybodyprism.com">support@mybodyprism.com</a>.
          </p>
          <p id="mbp-edu-waitlist-ok" class="form-ok" hidden role="status">
            You're on the list — we'll be in touch when it's ready.
          </p>
        </form>
      )
    }

    <p class="muted">
      PrismEducate is free, with no fixed end date. See the
      <a href="/legal/eula">EULA</a> and
      <a href="/legal/tos">Terms of Service</a> for the licence terms, and the
      <a href="/system-requirements">system requirements</a> before installing.
    </p>
  </section>

  {
    EDUCATE_DOWNLOADS_LIVE && (
      <script is:inline define:vars={{ educateEndpoint }}>
        // Download handler, same shape as /pricing's: POST the email, follow the
        // signed URL the API returns. Re-uses a still-valid link for the same
        // address instead of minting another, so a second click cannot create a
        // duplicate lead (the lesson from the viewer flow's 0ad99f1).
        (function () {
          var form = document.getElementById("mbp-edu-form");
          if (!form) return;
          var btn = document.getElementById("mbp-edu-btn");
          var err = document.getElementById("mbp-edu-error");
          var ok = document.getElementById("mbp-edu-ok");
          var cached = null;
          form.addEventListener("submit", function (event) {
            event.preventDefault();
            var email = (document.getElementById("mbp-edu-email").value || "").trim();
            if (!email || email.indexOf("@") < 1) {
              err.hidden = false;
              return;
            }
            err.hidden = true;
            if (cached && cached.email === email && Date.now() < cached.until) {
              window.location.href = cached.url;
              return;
            }
            btn.disabled = true;
            fetch(educateEndpoint, {
              method: "POST",
              headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
              body: JSON.stringify({ email: email }),
            })
              .then(function (response) {
                if (!response.ok) throw new Error("http " + response.status);
                return response.json();
              })
              .then(function (data) {
                if (!data || !data.download_url) throw new Error("no url");
                var ttl = (data.expires_in || 300) - 60;
                cached = {
                  email: email,
                  url: data.download_url,
                  until: Date.now() + ttl * 1000,
                };
                ok.hidden = false;
                window.location.href = data.download_url;
              })
              .catch(function () {
                err.hidden = false;
              })
              .then(function () {
                setTimeout(function () {
                  btn.disabled = false;
                }, 8000);
              });
          });
        })();
      </script>
    )
  }

  <style>
    .narrow { max-width: 760px; padding: 2.5rem 1.25rem 4rem; }
    .eyebrow {
      text-transform: uppercase;
      letter-spacing: 0.18em;
      font-size: 0.72rem;
      color: var(--c-brand);
      margin: 0 0 0.6rem;
    }
    h1 { margin: 0 0 1rem; }
    .lede { font-size: 1.08rem; margin-bottom: 2rem; }
    h2 { font-size: 1.15rem; margin: 2rem 0 0.75rem; }
    .organs {
      list-style: none;
      padding: 0;
      margin: 0 0 1rem;
      display: flex;
      flex-wrap: wrap;
      gap: 0.5rem;
    }
    .organs li {
      border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
      border-radius: 999px;
      padding: 0.3rem 0.85rem;
      font-size: 0.9rem;
      color: var(--c-text);
    }
    .muted { color: var(--c-muted); font-size: 0.92rem; }
    form { margin: 0 0 1.25rem; display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 0.6rem; align-items: flex-start; }
    input[type="email"] {
      width: 100%;
      max-width: 22rem;
      padding: 0.65rem 0.8rem;
      background: var(--c-bg-2);
      border: 1px solid var(--c-border);
      border-radius: 4px;
      color: var(--c-text);
      font: inherit;
    }
    .form-note, .form-error, .form-ok { font-size: 0.85rem; margin: 0; }
    .form-note { color: var(--c-muted); }
    .form-error { color: var(--c-warm); }
    .form-ok { color: var(--c-brand); }
    .visually-hidden {
      position: absolute;
      width: 1px;
      height: 1px;
      overflow: hidden;
      clip: rect(0 0 0 0);
      white-space: nowrap;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
